# Force LF line endings on checkout for all text files, on every platform.
#
# Prettier enforces LF (endOfLine: lf, its default) and the pre-commit hook
# runs `prettier --check` — so any file materialized with CRLF fails the hook
# until rewritten. Windows' core.autocrlf=true converts to CRLF whenever git
# touches a file (checkout, checkout-index, stash pop, ...), which made
# commits from Windows trip over formatting repeatedly. The `eol=lf` attribute
# overrides autocrlf, so checkouts are LF everywhere and the hook stays green.
#
# Binary files are unaffected: `text=auto` lets git detect and skip them.
* text=auto eol=lf
